From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:44:11 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: option to leave large arrays out of the numerical
 domains

Every byte of every array is a dimension of the numerical abstract state,
and the cost of each operation grows with the number of dimensions. With
"array_track_max_bytes": n (default -1, track all), the cells of arrays of
more than n bytes are not dimensions: assignments to them are dropped and
reads give the full range of the cell's type. Their initialization and the
bounds of indices into them are still checked. The option can only add
alarms.

Signed-off-by: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
